WEBVTT

00:10:57.103 --> 00:11:00.186
in a binary code,
and that's the defining trait

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:02.237
of the computer program.

00:11:02.261 --> 00:11:06.120
But we know that that's purely
syntactical. That's symbolic.

00:11:06.144 --> 00:11:10.135
We know that actual human consciousness
has something more than that.

00:11:10.159 --> 00:11:13.328
It's got a content
in addition to the syntax.

00:11:13.352 --> 00:11:14.825
It's got a semantics.

00:11:14.849 --> 00:11:17.314
Now that argument, I made
that argument 30 --

00:11:17.338 --> 00:11:18.605
oh my God, I don't want
to think about it —

00:11:18.629 --> 00:11:19.947
more than 30 years ago,

00:11:19.971 --> 00:11:22.876
but there's a deeper argument
implicit in what I've told you,

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.919
and I want to tell you that argument
briefly, and that is,

00:11:25.943 --> 00:11:30.069
consciousness creates
an observer-independent reality.